  "title": "The result: m c squared times gamma minus one",
  "spoken": "Integrating the longitudinal work from rest gives m c squared times gamma minus one.",
  "explanation": "Because the rate of change of gamma with speed is gamma cubed u over c squared, the integral is m c squared times the change in gamma, from 1 at rest to gamma at v. At 0.6c that is 0.25 m c squared; the familiar one half m v squared gives 0.18 m c squared, so at this speed the difference is plain.",
